1️⃣ INNER JOIN — only matching rows
Returns rows only when the join condition matches in BOTH tables.

SELECT title, domestic_sales, international_sales
FROM movies
  JOIN boxoffice
    ON movies.id = boxoffice.movie_id;
JOIN alone always means INNER JOIN (the word INNER is optional).
Rows with no match on the other side are dropped.
Practice
1. Find the domestic and international sales for each movie

SELECT title, domestic_sales, international_sales
FROM movies
  JOIN boxoffice
    ON movies.id = boxoffice.movie_id;
2. Show movies that did better internationally than domestically

SELECT title, domestic_sales, international_sales
FROM movies
  JOIN boxoffice
    ON movies.id = boxoffice.movie_id
WHERE domestic_sales < international_sales;
3. List all the movies by their ratings in descending order

SELECT title, domestic_sales, international_sales
FROM movies
  JOIN boxoffice
    ON movies.id = boxoffice.movie_id
ORDER BY rating DESC;
