FROM / JOIN  →  ON  →  WHERE  →  GROUP BY  →  HAVING  →  SELECT  →  ORDER BY  →  LIMIT
 (combine)     (match) (filter)   (group)     (filter     (project)   (sort)      (page)
                                                  groups)
✅ Recap card
JOIN type	Left unmatched	Right unmatched	Use when
INNER JOIN	❌ dropped	❌ dropped	You only need rows that exist in both
LEFT JOIN	✅ kept (NULLs)	❌ dropped	Left table is the "master" list
RIGHT JOIN	❌ dropped	✅ kept (NULLs)	Right table is the "master" list
FULL JOIN	✅ kept (NULLs)	✅ kept (NULLs)	You need everything from both
LEFT ANTI	✅ only unmatched	❌ dropped	Find left rows missing a match
RIGHT ANTI	❌ dropped	✅ only unmatched	Find right rows missing a match
CROSS JOIN	—	—	All combinations (Cartesian)
Key rules to remember:

JOIN = INNER JOIN.
OUTER JOIN keeps unmatched rows and fills the missing side with NULL.
Always IS NULL, never = NULL.
Anti join = OUTER JOIN + WHERE other_side IS NULL.
CROSS JOIN has no ON — it multiplies every row with every row.
